  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_021 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved the best accuracy (0.706) and F1 (0.667) at only 4.82 GPU hrs, a ~7% jump over the pca_n2000 baseline. The scvi_n200 RNA encoder + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion combination is clearly the strongest direction. Uncertainty: whether transformer aggregation can further improve over avgpool by better modeling inter-profile relationships in the multiprofile setting, especially with the richer scvi_n200 representations. This experiment (config_049) tests exactly that: it keeps all three best-performing components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) and swaps avgpool for transformer aggregation. It is the most direct and logical exploitation of the strongest signal found so far. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds moderate overhead over avgpool; I estimate ~8–12 GPU hrs, still well within budget and far cheaper than the anomalous 36.42-hr resnet50 run. With 5 experiments remaining, this high-value exploitation step is the best use of experiment 5."
}

